From 1c17e9e6106add80b59e281024dce604972048b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:00:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] backports: declare the NSS Wi-Fi offload symbols

The NSS patches each add their Kconfig symbols to local-symbols, so that
backports renames them to CPTCFG_ like its own. The ones ported from the
kernel tree no longer carry those hunks; declare all seven here instead.
---
 local-symbols | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/local-symbols b/local-symbols
index 7477209..2c88ee3 100644
--- a/local-symbols
+++ b/local-symbols
@@ -506,3 +506,10 @@ USB_WDM=
 USB_TMC=
 STAGING=
 RTL8723BS=
+ATH11K_DEBUGFS_HTT_STATS=
+ATH11K_DEBUGFS_STA=
+ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_256M=
+ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_512M=
+ATH11K_NSS_MESH_SUPPORT=
+ATH11K_NSS_SUPPORT=
+MAC80211_NSS_SUPPORT=
-- 
2.47.3

